{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:19-12","provision":"BCO 19-12","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"19-12","title":"Section 19-12","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/19-12/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/19-12","current_text":{"html":"<p>Presbyteries should require interns to devote themselves diligently to the trial of their gifts; and no one should be ordained to the work of the ministry of the Word until he has demonstrated the ability both to edify and to rule in the Church. Reports on every intern in the Presbytery should be presented at each stated meeting of the Presbytery by the committee of Presbytery charged with the oversight of interns, and these reports shall become a part of the minutes of Presbytery. The Presbytery shall also require every intern himself to make a report to it at least once a year describing his ministerial experiences. If the intern is still in school, the Presbytery shall secure from his instructors an annual report upon his deportment, diligence, and progress in study.</p>","text":"Presbyteries should require interns to devote themselves diligently to the trial of their gifts; and no one should be ordained to the work of the ministry of the Word until he has demonstrated the ability both to edify and to rule in the Church. Reports on every intern in the Presbytery should be presented at each stated meeting of the Presbytery by the committee of Presbytery charged with the oversight of interns, and these reports shall become a part of the minutes of Presbytery. The Presbytery shall also require every intern himself to make a report to it at least once a year describing his ministerial experiences. If the intern is still in school, the Presbytery shall secure from his instructors an annual report upon his deportment, diligence, and progress in study."},"source":{"name